        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(oauth): pass workspace context to resolveProviderIdForAuth on refresh failure",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a bug where an OAuth token refresh failure cleanup block (which deletes the cached profile snapshot entry when a refresh token expires or is rejected) fails to resolve workspace-scoped provider aliases correctly. This occurs because the cleanup call `resolveProviderIdForAuth(cred.provider)` lacks the optional `params` context containing `config` and `workspaceDir`, causing workspace-scoped provider mappings to resolve improperly and leave stale, broken credentials snapshots in the cache.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPropagated the `workspaceDir` parameter from entry points down to `resolveApiKeyForProfile` in `src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth.ts`.\n\nUpdated the refresh failure cleanup block to pass both `config` and `workspaceDir` to `resolveProviderIdForAuth` so workspace-specific provider resolution is preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\nEnsures workspace-scoped provider configurations correctly clean up cached credentials on refresh failures, preventing stale auth cache entries from blocking configuration adjustments.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPassed unit tests on branch `fix/1.4-oauth-resolve-provider-with-workspace`:\n```\n ✓ |unit-fast| src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-refresh-failure.test.ts (6 tests) 4ms\n```\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nVerified that running an OAuth refresh failure mock test correctly propagates the workspace configuration and removes the stale profile from `snapshot.lastGood`:\n```\n// Inside refresh failure handler:\nsnapshot.lastGood[providerKey] deleted successfully for workspace provider alias.\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/1.4-oauth-resolve-provider-with-workspace",
